{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations","id":951073,"title":"Changeling and Kinain Populations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-15T06:38:50-07:00","id":951073,"title":"Changeling and Kinain Populations","content":"I was wondering if we had an estimate of Changeling and Kinain populations? Given their relative weakness compared to vampires and werewolves, I think that Changelings could be 1:10,000 of the human population and Kinain could be 1:1,000 of the human population without really creating a world that much different than ours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T06:56:46-07:00","id":951082,"title":"","content":"Back when Babylon 5 was airing, the show's creator was extremely active on-line and would answer questions from fans. One that has always stuck with me was when a fan asked for specifics about how fast the ships on the show travel. His answer was at the speed of plot. How much time does it take to get from point A to point B? However much time the plot requires to be interesting and dramatic.<br /> <br /> That's the answer I think works best when questions about supernatural creature X populations crop up. How big of a population do you need for your chronicle to be interesting and fun? Does your plot require that changelings be so rare that a Kithain is lucky to meet more than a handful of other Kithain over the course of his life? Then in your chronicle, there's probably not going to more then a few per major urban area with most towns only having one or no changelings. Do you want a game with huge political rivalries and courts vying for territory? Then most cities in your chronicle will probably have enough changelings to fill out all roles in a couple of local courts and enough commoners to act as support and opposition for both. This might even make some small towns have as many changelings as humans, but as long as everyone at the table is willing to roll with it and having fun, I'd say go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T09:13:47-07:00","id":951148,"title":"","content":"So while I agree with the answer above, I also like assigning population numbers to get a general idea of a setting composition when I run games.<br /> <br /> I usually use 1 Changeling for every 20,000 humans and 1 Kinain for every 20 Changelings.<br /> This makes Changelings the second most populous Supernatural (after Wraiths) with all other splats assuming their on the brink of extinction (if not outright extinct) due to the Mists.<br /> <br /> And for the notion that Changelings are &quot;weaker&quot; than the other splats. I will assume you haven't actually played Changeling characters. In a number of games (at least 2) I've seen Changeling characters go one on one with Vampires, Gurahl, Garou and Mages. Changelings are terribly underestimated I find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:06:05-07:00","id":951207,"title":"","content":"Why would Kinain be less common than Changelings? It says in Enchanted, p. 13, that 80% of the children born to the mating of a Changeling with a mortal are Kinain (20% are Changelings) and that 50% of the children born to the mating of two Changelings are Kinain (50% are changelings), which would suggest that Kinain are at least three times as common as changelings. Add in the fact that the Faerie Blood can last for multiple generations, that the children and grandchildren of Kinain can be born Kinain, and I could easily see that the actually number of Kinain would be tenfold the number of Changelings.<br /> <br /> I have actually played Changeling, and they tend to fall apart fairly quickly because of Banality. That is especially true when they face Sorcerers, as Counterspells can easily shred cantrips, leaving the Changeling with nothing to show of their efforts (Mana is much easier to recover than Glamour). Where they excel is in the Dreaming, a Realm that few other creatures can enter, a Realm where the majority of changelings should probably dwell when they are not in the mortal world trying to breed more changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:25:36-07:00","id":951246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951207#post951207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would Kinain be less common than Changelings? It says in Enchanted, p. 13, that 80% of the children born to the mating of a Changeling with a mortal are Kinain (20% are Changelings) and that 50% of the children born to the mating of two Changelings are Kinain (50% are changelings), which would suggest that Kinain are at least three times as common as changelings. Add in the fact that the Faerie Blood can last for multiple generations, that the children and grandchildren of Kinain can be born Kinain, and I could easily see that the actually number of Kinain would be tenfold the number of Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The majority of Changelings are going to be Childlings which shouldn't be having any children. The Changelings most likely to have children are Grumps, who number the fewest. That skews the numbers a lot.<br /> Mind you, there aren't any hard numbers anywhere so this is entirely made up. If you want a quarter of the population to have fae blood, that's fine. I also tend to see Fae-Blooded (enough to qualify for the merit) having to be within a generation (possibly 2 if needed for story reasons)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:45:57-07:00","id":951254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951148#post951148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while I agree with the answer above, I also like assigning population numbers to get a general idea of a setting composition when I run games.<br /> <br /> I usually use 1 Changeling for every 20,000 humans and 1 Kinain for every 20 Changelings.<br /> This makes Changelings the second most populous Supernatural (after Wraiths) with all other splats assuming their on the brink of extinction (if not outright extinct) due to the Mists.<br /> <br /> And for the notion that Changelings are &amp;quot;weaker&amp;quot; than the other splats. I will assume you haven't actually played Changeling characters. In a number of games (at least 2) I've seen Changeling characters go one on one with Vampires, Gurahl, Garou and Mages. Changelings are terribly underestimated I find.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the 1:20,000 number has been stated elsewhere (Changeling ST's Guide, perhaps?), but I'd venture the number of kinain is higher. At least three times higher. <br /> <br /> Depending on your particular game, even dormant changelings, who have become Undone, can still spawn kinain (they still have a faerie soul - it's just asleep).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:00:57-07:00","id":951262,"title":"","content":"Strange, the majority of my Changeling games have revolved around Grumps, rather than Childlings or Wilders, because Childings grow up to be Wilders and Wilders grow up to be Grumps. The majority of the people who I played with also did not want to be treated like an inferior when they dealt with mortals and, even more important, Childlings begin with a Willpower 1 and Wilders begin with a Willpower 2, which makes both of them highly vulnerable to the effects of the powers of other supernatural creatures (Grumps start with Willpower 5). My players just reduced the difficulty of their Cantrips by using bunks, which made everything really, really fun to watch, and avoided temporary Banality by accepting Nightmare dice. I do not think that my players ever used Glamour to reduce the difficulty of their Cantrips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:43:46-07:00","id":951290,"title":"","content":"Well, maybe kinian are much more populated then Changelings. However, how much of them actually knows they are kinian? I am pretty sure that much less than Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:20:48-07:00","id":951338,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the children of Changelings know, but those with weaker blood likely do not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T15:58:36-07:00","id":951354,"title":"","content":"I imagine Changelings are the most common supernatural after wraiths because of well two things, first changelings have the most intricate base social structure there's a High King Of concordia, who has a parlament, and then there are multiple kings through out North america, who each have multiple Dukes who each have multiple Counts who each have multiple Barons all the way down to whole knightly orders. Meanwhile other groups generally have International and local with little in between, for Vampires its.. Prince then Justicar then Inner circle there's no &quot;Super prince/king/Emperor&quot; figure who might over see mutiple domains at once. <br /> <br /> Secondly you have descriptions in the Changeling Metaplot of a bunch of battles and these are at least hitting decent level SCA event numbers which even Sabbat Seiges or Hive raids don't seem to hit.<br /> <br /> And since changelings generally don't have to do much to cover things up they don't have to actively protect the Veil or Masquerade they can have a hidden large secodnary society.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T16:04:15-07:00","id":951359,"title":"","content":"I agree. The Mists protect them from mortals and, for the most part, they can retreat to the Near Dreaming if they need to do anything big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:34:31-07:00","id":951401,"title":"","content":"In short, changelings rock. <br /> <br /> Now gimme C20 already! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:54:52-07:00","id":951406,"title":"","content":"I am curious, how common are Childlings and Wilders in Changling games? Does their low Willpower matter much?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T18:55:46-07:00","id":951429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951406#post951406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious, how common are Childlings and Wilders in Changling games? Does their low Willpower matter much?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming the question is how often do people play Childlings and Wilders?<br /> About 25/75 for my games. I haven't had a player play a Grump yet. Having high willpower isn't super important. It's a stat like any other and I haven't had players feel the need to min/max their characters. Just going from memory, I think my player's wilder characters started with between 3 and 7.<br /> <br /> Also, it's a Changeling game after all. There aren't really any powers that target Willpower like in Vampire so the players are pressured less to have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:00:47-07:00","id":951434,"title":"","content":"Ah, you do not play crossover games then, I understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:09:36-07:00","id":951437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951434#post951434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, you do not play crossover games then, I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've run and played in plenty of crossover games. And it still doesn't matter. Creatures the players encounter don't know their stats. Like,a Vampires doesn't see a Changeling (they usually don't actually <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and say &quot;Hey, I'm going to target their Willpower since Changelings usually don't have much&quot;.<br /> <br /> Any Supernatural should be extremely cautious when they figure out that they're dealing with another Supernatural. None of them know what the others are capable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:58:10-07:00","id":951544,"title":"","content":"Plus, Willpower is cheap. I updated our game to Revised rules, so WP costs my players 1 Freebie per dot like any other critter.<br /> <br /> And yeah, other supernaturals can't even see fae unless they're trying and/or enchanted. That usually gives changelings the upper hand, since they get the element of surprise. Conversely, most changelings can see other supernaturals (except wraiths . . . unless they're sluagh) because chimerical reality warps around beings' psychological states, which makes vamps, mages, werewolves, etc, pretty obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T02:39:28-07:00","id":951570,"title":"","content":"Well, in terms of game mechanics changelins have as much willpower as other supernatural creatures. There is no age system in other settings, so we can take grump as base since mid 20s are grump years. Also, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5291_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5291\" data-vbnamecard=\"5291\">adambeyoncelowe</a> said, we can use Revised rules. That will pretty much sums up the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T05:57:13-07:00","id":951628,"title":"","content":"So, homebrew, got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:36:54-07:00","id":951736,"title":"","content":"Changeling never got a revised edition. I haven't seen C20 yet but I've always run it as Willpower costing 1 freebie, because that's how much it costs in literally every other character creation.<br /> <br /> But even without that, I find the idea that every player <i>needs</i> to buy up Willpower to high levels to be ridiculous. If Willpower 8+ is <i>required</i> then just have your players start with a higher base. If a stat is required for everyone to play, then everyone should get that stat to start.<br /> Most creatures in the WoD start with lower levels and that's fine. It is 100% okay to have a character with 4 or 5 Willpower because it makes sense for the character concept.<br /> <br /> And like I've said, I've played in and run plenty of crossovers and this has never been an issue for Changelings. Not from my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T08:46:57-07:00","id":951749,"title":"","content":"I do not think that I have ever played a character without Willpower 8+.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:00:04-07:00","id":951794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951749#post951749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that I have ever played a character without Willpower 8+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not?<br /> And to meet the character requirements, why do you think Willpower 8+ is necessary?<br /> Admittedly this is a tangent, but I would guess all who were going to weigh in on the OP have done so already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T10:57:02-07:00","id":951837,"title":"","content":"Well, I do not think that weak willed people can do anything to change the course of events in the World of Darkness (though I realize that Changelings have their own eccentricities) because Willpower, in many ways, is a representation of how much you can influence the world around you. For example, a Willpower 3 Kindred is nothing more than a joke to his neighboring vampires because he is such an easy tool to use. He is vulnerable to Dominate and Presence and to the middle levels of many other Disciplines (Animalism 3 and Auspex 4 come to mind), and he is incapable of ever being effective at Blood Magic. He is also unable to project his will on the world because he only has three potential automatic successes and only rolls three dice with Willpower rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:19:01-07:00","id":951857,"title":"","content":"I have never seen Willpower as a reflection of potential to influence the world.<br /> <br /> It's a stat like any other. Garou (and every other shifter besides Gurahl) start with 3-5. Changelings with 1-5. Vampires with 2-5. Mages and Wraiths start with 5, because they are strong willed. 5 is Strong willed. Higher than that is moreso. 8+ is very much not necessary. My first Werewolf character ended the game at Rank 4 with 6 I think.<br /> Even just from a mechanical standpoint, you don't need automatic successes to be awesome or to accomplish amazing things.<br /> I use them in dire circumstances when I need a little boost. If you can't accomplish something without Willpower expenditure, than there is a decent chance you shouldn't have been attempting it in the first place.<br /> Other characters....my 900 year old Ravnos ended the game with 8 or 9 Willpower. He started with 5 or 6. It was never an issue.<br /> My Tzimisce Voivode started with 8 and ended the game with 9 or 10.<br /> Strider Metis Galliard started with 6, ended with 7.<br /> Sidhe Childling started with 3. Ended the game with 5.<br /> <br /> And so on and so on.<br /> It just really isn't required to have high Willpower ratings. Not in my opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T11:28:42-07:00","id":951861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951749#post951749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that I have ever played a character without Willpower 8+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you start with Stamina, Dexterity and Strength all at 5 too? And Brawl, Melee and Firearms? And Generation/Arete/Dharma/Rank? And Resources? Only rich, combat munchkin elders really have any power to make a difference in the World of Darkness, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T12:02:19-07:00","id":951895,"title":"","content":"Not at all, but they are not individually as important as Willpower in most of the WoD (and it is impossible to create a beginning character with maximum Attribute spreads). I will, however, have my most important Attribute and Ability for my characters at 4 or 5 because you are supposed to be exceptional at something as a PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:18:55-07:00","id":951960,"title":"","content":"I think it really does depend on the critter. Vampires use Willpower a lot, so it makes sense to buy it up. Wraiths already begin with high Willpower. Mages begin with high Willpower but it's better to make it even higher. But for changelings, it's probably more important to buy up your Glamour, your Realms and your Backgrounds. Glamour and Banality are far more important traits in the game than Willpower. <br /> <br /> Unlike Disciplines or Spheres, possessing Arts alone isn't enough to be able to do magic. You need to have a decent spread in Realms or your effects are really limited. It doesn't help that Second Edition Arts are broken, so players have to spend a lot of time thinking about how the combination of Arts and Realms they're choosing works, which encourages min-maxing. If they don't pick right, they can end up with a mix of powers that are next to useless. <br /> <br /> Glamour is also very scarce, so you either want to buy more permanent Glamour or make up for the lack of flexibility in your magical prowess with some Backgrounds instead (Treasures offer an easy fix if you can't spend Freebies on both Arts and Realms; Remembrance opens up the possibility of boosting all combat dice pools; Chimera lets you take multiple chimerical items of equal or lesser value, so you can get armour and weapons together by investing a few dots in one trait).<br /> <br /> Rather than Willpower, Title is a better investment if you want to resist Sovereign (it's like Generation and Dominate in that respect). There aren't many other important things you'll need Willpower for. In fact, it rarely gets rolled in the CTD game I run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-16-2016, 04:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:24:01-07:00","id":951965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951895#post951895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all, but they are not individually as important as Willpower in most of the WoD (and it is impossible to create a beginning character with maximum Attribute spreads). I will, however, have my most important Attribute and Ability for my characters at 4 or 5 because you are supposed to be exceptional at something as a PC.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really strikes me at least as setting out to min/max (at least a little). Almost no character concept <i>needs</i> 4 or 5s in their &quot;important&quot; Attributes and Abilities, for a minimum or 8 dice pools. Starting characters aren't really supposed to be close to being the best in the world. This obviously might just be my opinion. I don't see where you have room to grow starting out like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:27:03-07:00","id":951968,"title":"","content":"A permanent Glamour of 5 would probably be useful, but you can also exploit bunks to reduce difficulty without using Glamour and use Nightmare Dice instead of spending Glamour to neutralize temporary banality. I would think that Willpower would still be useful in Changeling though, especially if you have crossover games.<br /> <br /> You grow through diversifying your character. No beginning character is good at everything, but they should be good at something. Why else were they granted supernatural capabilities, if they are not exceptional?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:40:04-07:00","id":951981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951968#post951968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You grow through diversifying your character. No beginning character is good at everything, but they should be good at something. Why else were they granted supernatural capabilities, if they are not exceptional?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the game you're playing. Vampires are really the only ones that pick people to become Vampires.<br /> Also, it seems your definition of being good at something, and correct me if I'm wrong, is having 8+ dice pool in said thing. To me, 8+ is being one of the best. Starting characters generally aren't. For my games, a good fighter would probably have 6 or 7 dice to Brawl and Athletics. You can build up from there over the course of the game. Any Abilities at 4+ need a <i>very good</i> explanation at character creation to be allowed.<br /> <br /> Characters are already exceptional given their Attribute and Ability spreads. 7/5/3 represents someone exceptional given that 2 in an Attribute is average.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:58:29-07:00","id":951996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951968#post951968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A permanent Glamour of 5 would probably be useful, but you can also exploit bunks to reduce difficulty without using Glamour and use Nightmare Dice instead of spending Glamour to neutralize temporary banality. I would think that Willpower would still be useful in Changeling though, especially if you have crossover games.<br /> <br /> You grow through diversifying your character. No beginning character is good at everything, but they should be good at something. Why else were they granted supernatural capabilities, if they are not exceptional?</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, which is why spending on Arts and Realms is such a tricky thing in CTD. You have to know in advance who or what exactly you plan to use each Art on before you can spend your dots. If you don't choose well, you'll find you have an Art that can only be used in very limited circumstances or not at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:42:51-07:00","id":952290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=951996#post951996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, which is why spending on Arts and Realms is such a tricky thing in CTD. You have to know in advance who or what exactly you plan to use each Art on before you can spend your dots. If you don't choose well, you'll find you have an Art that can only be used in very limited circumstances or not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IF only there were a revised edition....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T05:53:42-07:00","id":952449,"title":"","content":"Well, White Wolf did not see the profit in it. I would have much rather had a Changeling Revised than Demon or Orpheus, but White Wolf was addicted to bringing out more lines instead of developing existing ones because they were always chasing the next Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T06:48:12-07:00","id":952478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952449#post952449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, White Wolf did not see the profit in it. I would have much rather had a Changeling Revised than Demon or Orpheus, but White Wolf was addicted to bringing out more lines instead of developing existing ones because they were always chasing the next Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> C20 is supposed to bring things up to revised level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T07:09:21-07:00","id":952488,"title":"","content":"Hopefully. I am not really anticipating anything soon though, I still have not gotten my Exalted 3rd edition Kickstarter book, and it was supposed to be delivered in October 2013. I would not be surprised if C20 is not similarly delayed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T08:25:39-07:00","id":952535,"title":"","content":"All of the writing on C20 has been done for months. It's finished with the development pass, and the text is with the editor and art director right now as seen in the Monday Meeting blogs. There's always a chance something crazy and unexpected might happen with editing, art direction, layout, or White Wolf approvals, but so far, C20 is chugging right along to completion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T08:46:14-07:00","id":952552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952535#post952535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the writing on C20 has been done for months. It's finished with the development pass, and the text is with the editor and art director right now as seen in the Monday Meeting blogs. There's always a chance something crazy and unexpected might happen with editing, art direction, layout, or White Wolf approvals, but so far, C20 is chugging right along to completion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because it directly applies to the above conversation and I think it is probably not a huge deal to ask, would you be able to say if Willpower cost 1 freebie or 2 in C20 (as of now)?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T09:50:42-07:00","id":952575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952552#post952552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just because it directly applies to the above conversation and I think it is probably not a huge deal to ask, would you be able to say if Willpower cost 1 freebie or 2 in C20 (as of now)?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm betting 100% it costs the same as every other oWoD game: 1 freebie per dot. <br /> <br /> This is the one rulebook I'm most excited about. Wr20 will be good too, but Wraith was pretty consistently good, and the rules were pretty solid. Changeling needed so many bandages the game came out looking more like a mummy than Mummy. :P<br /> <br /> Arts and Realms definitely look promising. The system seems simpler and we have Unleashing now. We also appear to have a much wider range of Arts. With Unleashing, I'd be surprised if most PCs stuck to the rather limited cantrips of a linear Arts system and didn't just go for a wilder, freeform option of frequent Unleashings. I know I would.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in seeing how the Glamour economy gets fixed, as well as subsystems such as Reverie, Dragon's Ire, Kenning, and the Birthrights and Frailties, too. <br /> <br /> Anyone know if we're likely to see a PDF any time soon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-17-2016, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:03:34-07:00","id":952582,"title":"","content":"I'm happy to talk about things that have already been revealed, and when the game comes out, I'll certainly be willing talk about my thought process behind my sections if anyone is interested. It's not my place to reveal anything that hasn't already been revealed though.<br /> <br /> That being said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a> has said a few times he's willing to answer C20 questions. I'm pretty surprised how few people have taken him up on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952575#post952575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arts and Realms definitely look promising. The system seems simpler and we have Unleashing now. We also appear to have a much wider range of Arts. With Unleashing, I'd be surprised if most PCs stuck to the rather limited cantrips of a linear Arts system and didn't just go for a wilder, freeform option of frequent Unleashings. I know I would.<br /> <br /> I'm also interested in seeing how the Glamour economy gets fixed, as well as subsystems such as Reverie, Dragon's Ire, Kenning, and the Birthrights and Frailties, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why I can't wait for the book to get into people's hands. All of this is so incredibly cool! And here I am, stuck, unable to say why Unleashing probably won't be used constantly (but when it is, it'll almost certainly be memorable!) or talk about the fifth R or the Dauntain or Bedlam or [REDACTED] that hasn't even been hinted at anywhere yet. I mean.... the Time Realm you guys, the <b>Time Realm</b>!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":".  Adding a response to adambeyoncelowe. 08-17-2016, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T10:19:40-07:00","id":952596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952582#post952582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy to talk about things that have already been revealed, and when the game comes out, I'll certainly be willing talk about my thought process behind my sections if anyone is interested. It's not my place to reveal anything that hasn't already been revealed though.<br /> <br /> That being said, <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> has said a few times he's willing to answer C20 questions. I'm pretty surprised how few people have taken him up on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's because he's not been on here much, perhaps? Rich Dansky pops up on the Wraith boards a lot, so he gets inundated. People are probably shy/nervous about PMing a developer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T04:27:35-07:00","id":953092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952488#post952488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully. I am not really anticipating anything soon though, I still have not gotten my Exalted 3rd edition Kickstarter book, and it was supposed to be delivered in October 2013. I would not be surprised if C20 is not similarly delayed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exalted is itsown scenario, and Wraith is actually cursed. I am expecting c20 pdf before the end of the year, with my most optimistic saying the end of the Wiccan year...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T12:25:42-07:00","id":953348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952582#post952582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is why I can't wait for the book to get into people's hands. All of this is so incredibly cool! And here I am, stuck, unable to say why Unleashing probably won't be used constantly (but when it is, it'll almost certainly be memorable!) or talk about the fifth R or the Dauntain or Bedlam or [REDACTED] that hasn't even been hinted at anywhere yet. I mean.... the Time Realm you guys, the <b>Time Realm</b>!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the fifth R has been mentioned in the kith write-ups we've already seen. So Reverie, Rapture, Ravaging, Rhapsody and Revelry. I'm assuming the last is a way for a changeling to gather Glamour from a group activity, but perhaps specific to each kith (IIRC, the sample kith write-ups we saw gave each kith a unique way to garner Glamour via Revelry). It makes sense, at least. A satyr can throw a party or an orgy. A troll can lead a band of soldiers in battle for duty. A sluagh can lead a group to silence or secrecy. An eshu can engage a group in storytelling. Or whatever. It seems like a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T12:39:01-07:00","id":953355,"title":"","content":"How will greater access to Glamour change things? The games that I ran (and played in) were very dependent on bunks to reduce difficulty and Nightmare Dice to negate banality because of a relative lack of Glamour. Glamour was used for Enchanting and for Wyrd, not for reducing difficulty or negating temporary Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T18:03:03-07:00","id":953528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=953355#post953355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How will greater access to Glamour change things? The games that I ran (and played in) were very dependent on bunks to reduce difficulty and Nightmare Dice to negate banality because of a relative lack of Glamour. Glamour was used for Enchanting and for Wyrd, not for reducing difficulty or negating temporary Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Greater access to Glamour lets you do more magic. Thus you can avoid Nightmare Dice a bit more and it's slightly easier to Call on the Wyrd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T02:07:12-07:00","id":953723,"title":"","content":"re: the scarcity of Glamour--what makes it so scarce? Can't it be harvested from experiencing beauty and the creation thereof, like the Toreador Clan weakness through a mirror brightly? It's been awhile since I read Changeling so I don't remember exactly how Glamour works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T03:34:44-07:00","id":953743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=953723#post953723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">re: the scarcity of Glamour--what makes it so scarce? Can't it be harvested from experiencing beauty and the creation thereof, like the Toreador Clan weakness through a mirror brightly? It's been awhile since I read Changeling so I don't remember exactly how Glamour works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Experiencing it? Not really. Some items emit tiny amounts of Glamour long after creation, but mostly changelings in CTD1e/2e have to inspire the *creation* of an artwork, gaining a handful of Glamour for days, weeks or, more often, months of hard work. They can gain a few more by *destroying* a valuable work of art, but that's a one-time thing. Then they can drain the Glamour inherent in dreamers, but it's frowned upon, and risks permanently damaging the human. <br /> <br /> Most of CTD is about myths and fairytales, but changelings don't actually gain Glamour that way. It's almost like they tacked on this idea of Glamour-as-art, but made it pretty much the only way to get Glamour, despite it not being as central to the game as the idea of tapping into mythic threads.<br /> <br /> Relvery sounds like it fits better, because of that. Fae should get Glamour by being fae and getting into adventures, as much as they get it from living in artists' communes and living the bohemian lifestyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T05:37:39-07:00","id":953763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=952582#post952582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm happy to talk about things that have already been revealed, and when the game comes out, I'll certainly be willing talk about my thought process behind my sections if anyone is interested. It's not my place to reveal anything that hasn't already been revealed though.<br /> <br /> That being said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a> has said a few times he's willing to answer C20 questions. I'm pretty surprised how few people have taken him up on that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And this is why I can't wait for the book to get into people's hands. All of this is so incredibly cool! And here I am, stuck, unable to say why Unleashing probably won't be used constantly (but when it is, it'll almost certainly be memorable!) or talk about the fifth R or the Dauntain or Bedlam or [REDACTED] that hasn't even been hinted at anywhere yet. I mean.... the Time Realm you guys, the <b>Time Realm</b>!</div> </div> </div> </div>What are these sections of yours? If we can know them, we can talk about it. I am pretty sure &quot;pooka&quot; is your section <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:26:49-07:00","id":953784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KokoroWatari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=953763#post953763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are these sections of yours? If we can know them, we can talk about it. I am pretty sure &quot;pooka&quot; is your section <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>This thread is getting super off-topic &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> The Pooka write-up wasn't me. It was done by someone far more appropriate - the Grand Pooka himself! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I had the Courts (Seelie, Unseelie, and Shadow), Traits (Legacies, Attributes, Abilities, Backgrounds, Willpower, Glamour, Banality, and Health), Thallain background and mechanics, and the Korred, Morganed, Wichtel, and Wolpertinger kith write-ups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:28:02-07:00","id":953787,"title":"","content":"To get it back on topic, how often do you use Kinain in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:51:43-07:00","id":953807,"title":"","content":"Helping to get back on topic, I don't use them a whole lot. When they do get used in games I run, it's always been as an NPC so far. The last major chronicle I ran had a prominent NPC Kinain who was the sister of one of the PCs. The look on the players' faces was absolutely priceless when it dawned on them that she was actually fae-blooded and knew what the characters were really up the entire time! She just never made a big deal about it because she grew up around it all going on around her and so it seemed normal to her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T09:25:33-07:00","id":953880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=953787#post953787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To get it back on topic, how often do you use Kinain in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>I used them a lot in my chronicle. However, they were always in background, doing something secret or hideous. I run my game for 2 years, 1381, 1863 and 1969. They were active in 69 because of resurgence. I will resume my chronicle in September and they will reincarnate in 99. Then, I will toss a lot Kinian on them.<br /> <br /> They could be the major factor to hide kithians life. For example, you can be a ceo and take kithians and provide a work space for them without causing any other problem to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7562-kokorowatari","name":"KokoroWatari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T10:50:09-07:00","id":953910,"title":"","content":"Thanks Adam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T11:11:29-07:00","id":953920,"title":"","content":"I'm running a crossover game with Mage, so I encourage mages with Fae Blood and Faerie Affinity. It just makes everything easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:01:37-07:00","id":953976,"title":"","content":"I actually think that the two Merits work better for Sorcerers than Mages, as Changelings tend to be nervous around Mages (competition for resources, as Glamour is a form of Quintessence) and as Mages cannot develop anything that requires Glamour, but I can see the point of a crossover game. After all, Changelings are the most common major supernatural other than Wraiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T13:55:12-07:00","id":954021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=953920#post953920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a crossover game with Mage, so I encourage mages with Fae Blood and Faerie Affinity. It just makes everything easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its just mind one, spirit 1!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T01:47:06-07:00","id":954276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=954021#post954021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its just mind one, spirit 1!</div> </div> </div> </div>To see chimerical reality, yes. But to interact with the Dreaming itself requires other Spheres. Plus, giving a character fae heritage means all this is part of their Paradigm--I mean, how many Sons of Ether know to tune into chimerical reality to check if the weird person in front of them is actually fae? <br /> <br /> It helps that one of the Big Bads was actually a Marauder from House Merinita. <br /> <br /> Also, the rules for enchantment in First and Second Edition are so unclear and unforgiving. You get enchanted for a day and then fall into a coma for weeks when it wears off... This way, there's a degree of handwaving and characters are encouraged to stay together. <br /> <br /> The final reason I've allowed it is because now the kinain mage PC can work on a Fae Minor Sphere, which we're both quite excited about. <br /> <br /> We used to have two kinain mages but now we just have one Hollower who was descended from fae and uses some of their styles in his own gutter magick. The other two mages have joined the fae because of a shared hatred of the Technocracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:01:19-07:00","id":956607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/951073-changeling-and-kinain-populations?p=954276#post954276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To see chimerical reality, yes. But to interact with the Dreaming itself requires other Spheres. Plus, giving a character fae heritage means all this is part of their Paradigm--I mean, how many Sons of Ether know to tune into chimerical reality to check if the weird person in front of them is actually fae?<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically in the game I'm in the Etherite i'm playing basically had to explain to the Verbena and Hermetic how to see into the Dreaming.. Ufology, Fortean phenomenia, Parapsychology, the Hollow Earth etc are all parts and parcel to the Etherites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T16:39:38-07:00","id":956622,"title":"","content":"I do like the Sons of Ether...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T22:41:10-07:00","id":956795,"title":"","content":"I do too. One of our characters is an Etherite construct known as Tom Morrow, the Man of Tomorrow. I guess he feels some kind of affinity (lower-case A) with the fae. Recently, he's been getting on better with them than the mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}